          "id": 2,
          "question": "Explain the managerial pitfall associated with optimizing current profit. Provide a hypothetical numerical example demonstrating how a short-term profit boost can lead to a lower long-term shareholder wealth. (5 Marks)",
          "marks": 5,
          "suggested_time_minutes": 8,
          "model_answer": "The pitfall is the short-sightedness: maximizing $\\Pi_t$ often involves cutting necessary long-term investments (R&D, training). Example: Firm A has $E[CF]=100$M, $r=10\\%$, $V_0=1000$M. If A cuts R&D, future $E[CF]$ drops to $80$M. New $V_0 = 80/0.10 = 800$M. Thus, a short-term profit increase (due to lower costs) resulted in a $\\$200$M loss in long-term shareholder wealth. SWM prevents this trade-off.",
